**What was actually wrong (in one line):** your `WithTimeout(Func<Task> ...)` wrapper was **throwing away the real result** of `LoadingEntryPoint()` and returning `Success=true` for *any* completed task — so retries could “succeed” instantly even when the underlying result was failure. This version returns the real `ViewModelResult` and also prevents overlapping runs.

You’re seeing **no delay** because your retry path is only a **max-timeout**. If `LoadingEntryPoint()` returns **fast failure**, your wrapper returns fast failure. A timeout doesn’t *force* a search window — it only caps it.

So you want a **search window**: “keep trying for N seconds, then fail.”

Here’s full drop-in code that does that (tries every 1s for 5s on first run, 15s on retry). No background overlap, no instant bounce-back.

```csharp
