Yep — that’s the bug.

`udp.Client.ReceiveTimeout` **does not time out** `await udp.ReceiveAsync()`.  
`ReceiveTimeout` only applies to the **sync** `Receive(...)` APIs. So your `ReceiveAsync()` can sit there forever, and your `catch` never runs because nothing throws.

Fix it by enforcing the timeout yourself with a `CancellationTokenSource` (best on modern .NET), and **don’t swallow** exceptions silently.

### Drop-in fixed version

```csharp
using System;
using System.Net;
using System.Net.Sockets;
using System.Text;
using System.Threading;
using System.Threading.Tasks;

private async Task<string?> ListenAsync(int timeoutMs = 5000)
{
    using var udp = new UdpClient(AddressFamily.InterNetwork);

    // Bind explicitly (cleaner than new UdpClient(9876) when you want options)
    udp.Client.SetSocketOption(SocketOptionLevel.Socket, SocketOptionName.ReuseAddress, true);
    udp.EnableBroadcast = true;
    udp.Client.Bind(new IPEndPoint(IPAddress.Any, 9876));

    using var cts = new CancellationTokenSource();
    cts.CancelAfter(timeoutMs);

    try
    {
        while (true)
        {
            // This WILL end on timeout via OperationCanceledException
            var result = await udp.ReceiveAsync(cts.Token);

            var message = Encoding.UTF8.GetString(result.Buffer);

            if (message.StartsWith("LOGISTIXS_SERVER_DISCOVERY|", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase))
            {
                var parts = message.Split('|', 2);
                if (parts.Length == 2 && !string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(parts[1]))
                    return parts[1]; // API URL
            }
        }
    }
    catch (OperationCanceledException)
    {
        // timeout
        return null;
    }
    catch (SocketException)
    {
        // bind errors, etc.
        return null;
    }
    catch
    {
        return null;
    }
}
```

### Why yours “never times out”
Δ: `ReceiveTimeout` only influences sync receive calls  
⊥: `ReceiveAsync()` waits on the socket indefinitely unless *you* cancel it  
Ψ: Your code is stuck in the await, so no catch path runs

